+- Fonts via `next/font/google` **or** `next/font/local`, ONE file per
+  family, subset to `SUBSET_CHARSET` (`apps/orchestrator/src/design/faces.ts`)
+  rather than to Google's `latin` + `latin-ext` pair — ş/ğ/ı/İ/ç/ö/ü must
+  render, confirmed by rendering them, not by trusting a catalogue page.
+  `faces.turkish.test.ts` is that confirmation: it renders every vendored
+  face in a browser and fails on any character that arrives from the
+  fallback. At most two display/body families plus an optional monospace
+  accent. Which faces are permitted is
   the direction's decision (D10 §3.2, §11 C1/C3). Self-hosted faces are free
   open-licence faces only — no foundry licence is bought, so a per-domain or
   pageview-capped licence disqualifies a face (D10 §13 Q2).
